  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0743">Definition <span data-tag="0743">11.2.5</span>.</a> Given a $k$-algebra $A$ we denote $A^{op}$ the $k$-algebra we get by reversing the order of multiplication in $A$. This is called the <em>opposite algebra</em>. </p>
